<title>USA: Gensia Sicor places $20 million in notes.</title>
<headline>Gensia Sicor places $20 million in notes.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gensia Sicor Inc said Friday it signed an agreement with Health Care Capital Partners LP, a fund managed by Ferrer Freeman Thompson &amp; Co LLC, for the private placement of $20 million in convertible notes due in 2004.</p>
<p>The company said the notes are convertible into preferred or common stock at a price of $3.78 per share and include warrants to purchase up to 2,645,503 shares of its common stock at $4.35 per share.</p>
<p>The notes bear a coupon of 2.675 percent, Gensia said.</p>
